' ===========================================================================
' Built-in `app::` package source (plan-62-A).
'
' Declares the `Mode` enum that names an `--app` program's *presentation mode* —
' what its window surface currently is. `app::getMode` / `app::setMode` (native
' inline builtins) read and write the per-execution-context presentation-mode
' field; this source only provides the enum type so `Mode.Console` / `Mode.None`
' resolve. The two callables are lowered directly in native codegen (plan-62-B),
' exactly like `money::getRounding` / `money::setRounding`.
'
' The enum discriminants are exactly the stored values: `Console = 0` (the
' terminal-in-a-window surface that exists today, the default) and `None = 1`
' (windowless). A future `GUI` / `Canvas` mode is a new variant appended here.
' ===========================================================================

DOC
  ENUM Mode
  DESC Names an `--app` program's presentation mode — what its window surface
  DESC currently is. Set the mode with `app::setMode` and read it with
  DESC `app::getMode`.
  PROP Console The terminal-in-a-window surface (the default).
  PROP None Windowless — no surface is presented.
END DOC
EXPORT ENUM Mode
  Console         ' the terminal-in-a-window surface (default)
  None            ' windowless
END ENUM
